+# Feature Specification: JSON Merge Patch
+
+**Input**: Implement RFC 7386: export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`; returns the merged document.
+
+## Requirements
+- A non-object patch (primitive, array, `null`) replaces the target entirely.
+- An object patch is merged into the target; a non-object target is treated as `{}`.
+- Patch members with `null` delete the target member; other members merge recursively.
+- Arrays are replaced, never merged. Nulls nested in patch values that are added to a non-object are dropped (RFC pseudo-code).
+- Inputs are never mutated, and the result shares no structure with them.
+- A `__proto__` member is plain data.
+
+## Verification
+`test/mergepatch.test.ts` covers all RFC 7386 Appendix A cases, non-mutation, and `__proto__`.
